xnu 0416: a released IOSurface view keeps its state page, not the surface

trapRelease() keeps the last 256 released views of a client so that their state page stays mapped (backboardd reads a
surface's seed through another framework client after one is released). The kept view also kept its reference to the
surface: a "CA Framebuffer" or "CA Asynchronous Page" CoreAnimation had let go stayed alive, and with it its slot of
the scanout pool, until 256 more views were released or backboardd exited. Measured on 2026-11-19 with 0415's census:
slots of surfaces "NOT in the table, refs 1, GPU buffers 0" -- the kept view's reference alone -- filled the pool, the
ring's next framebuffer was made outside it (linear) and every frame went the copy's way; restarting backboardd freed
seven slots of eight.

The kept view now drops the surface once it has given up its use of it; its own map of the state page holds the page.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
index 10bf9da..9f6a86c 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -1802,6 +1802,7 @@ IOReturn
 IOSurfaceRootUserClient::trapRelease(void *id, void *, void *, void *, void *, void *)
 {
 	unsigned int index;
+	SweetSurface *gone = NULL;          /* 0416 */
 	IOLockLock(fLock);
 	SweetSurfaceRef *ref = findRef((uint32_t)(uintptr_t)id, &index, true);
 	if (ref == NULL) {
@@ -1818,6 +1819,14 @@ IOSurfaceRootUserClient::trapRelease(void *id, void *, void *, void *, void *, v
 		 */
 		OSSafeReleaseNULL(ref->data);
 		sweet_surface_put(ref->surface);
+		/*
+		 * 0416: the kept view holds its state page (its own map of it), not the surface. Holding the surface kept a
+		 * window server's released "CA Framebuffer" alive -- and its slot of the scanout pool taken -- until 256 more
+		 * views were released or backboardd exited: the pool filled with surfaces no program had, the ring's next one
+		 * was made outside it, and every frame went the copy's way.
+		 */
+		gone = ref->surface;
+		ref->surface = NULL;
 		ref->released = true;
 		ref->detached = false;
 		if (fZombies != NULL && fZombies->setObject(ref)) {
@@ -1828,6 +1837,7 @@ IOSurfaceRootUserClient::trapRelease(void *id, void *, void *, void *, void *, v
 		fRefs->removeObject(index);
 	}
 	IOLockUnlock(fLock);
+	OSSafeReleaseNULL(gone);            /* 0416: (outside fLock: the last reference frees it, and its pool slot) */
 	return ref != NULL ? kIOReturnSuccess : kIOReturnNotFound;
 }
 
